# Backend architecture (required)

Before editing Go under `backend/`, read [backend/AGENTS.md](backend/AGENTS.md).

## Structure (do not collapse layers)

- **Handlers:** `internal/api/{domain}/handler.go` + `dto/` + `dto/mapper/`
- **Services:** `internal/{domain}/service.go` + `domain/`
- **Repos:** `internal/{domain}/storage/repository.go` (exported `Repository`, raw pgx SQL)
- **Router:** register routes in `internal/http/router/router.go` — not per-feature `Mount()`
- **DI:** wire in `cmd/api/main.go` only
- **Shared:** `pkg/commonlibrary/{render,request,errors,db}`, `internal/middleware/`

## Non-negotiables

- API errors must stay `{ "code", "message", "fields"? }` via `pkg/commonlibrary/errors`
- No flat `internal/foo/` packages mixing handler + service + repo
- Handlers call services only — never import `internal/*/storage`
- Services depend on service-owned interfaces, never on `*storage.Repository`, `pgxpool`, or `pgx.Tx`; use `commondb.TxRunner` for atomic writes (see AGENTS.md guardrail 5)
- Services return `*apperr.Error` / sentinels (`pkg/commonlibrary/apperr`); handlers use `commonerrors.WriteError` (maps via `FromError`); never import `commonlibrary/errors` in services (see AGENTS.md guardrail 8)
- Entities own lifecycle rules: billing/payment status transitions are decided by `domain.Group` methods; storage only persists them with compare-and-set, never status literals or `CASE` (see AGENTS.md guardrail 9)
- Camp-admin writes go through `internal/campadmin` use cases that own audit recording; handlers and middleware must not call `adminlog.Recorder` (see AGENTS.md guardrail 10)
- No sqlboiler/goose/viper/zap unless explicitly requested
- `/camp-admin/stream` stays outside request-timeout middleware

## New work checklist

1. Domain types → `internal/{domain}/domain/`
2. Service method → `internal/{domain}/service.go`
3. Storage (if needed) → `internal/{domain}/storage/`
4. DTOs + mappers → `internal/api/{domain}/dto/`
5. Handler method → `internal/api/{domain}/handler.go`
6. Route → `internal/http/router/router.go`
7. `go build ./... && go test ./...`

Reference implementations: `registration` (full), `camp` (minimal reads).
